{"title":"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 27","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_27\">Problem 27</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 27\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An ordered pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/4/cf47a1a180424fc2d150cfb2e9f0d95b7a717927.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$( b , c )$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> of integers, each of which has absolute value less than or equal to five, is chosen at random, with each\nsuch ordered pair having an equal likelihood of being chosen. What is the probability that the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/5/745595c3e71280acc944ea1c590d8f1e1eae0ed1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^ 2 + bx + c = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"121\" height=\"16\" /> will\nnot have distinct positive real roots?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/8/928fa2f35aac1bf50df0c90531dfb04ad18fdc73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{106}{121}\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }\\frac{108}{121}\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }\\frac{110}{121}\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }\\frac{112}{121}\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }\\text{none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"528\" height=\"38\" />    \n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/2/55206bce678ac0394d97dc04dd72398df2bdf572.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{E}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" /> \n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cases where the roots are real, positive and distinct.\nThe roots to the quadratic equation are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/5/7b535ddd6e94c7a009908738d0fe6365c2301d5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{-b\\pm\\sqrt{b^2-4c}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"116\" height=\"40\" />. \n</p><p>In order for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/e/f4e97bc7a326b7afb640edf9c04771a7585fd22f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-b-\\sqrt{b^2-4c}&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" /> we certainly need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/c/0ecb51168110ad94dd985867b53aac5f34b2e9dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />.\nAdditionally, for the roots to be both real and distinct we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/c/2bc82d2c615cf884fe4b914cfd0a0d6b1cd24d42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2-4c&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"87\" height=\"15\" />. And lastly, for both roots to be positive we\nneed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/d/a5dd6b6b640a354198129f9f032e68f5861b08ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-b&gt;\\sqrt{b^2-4c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"118\" height=\"21\" />. Combining these inequalities we determine that  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/e/78e9ef328a5077e5e76a7e1b0bf77401bf6b5422.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{b^2}{4}&gt;c&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"84\" height=\"39\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/c/0ecb51168110ad94dd985867b53aac5f34b2e9dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p>This leaves just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cases <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/c/c8c2518434e6b68ed23f6afcaef536dc68d13f60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{(-5,1),(-5,2)(-5,3),(-5,4),(-5,5),(-4,1),(-4,2),(-4,3),(-3,1),(-3,2)\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"627\" height=\"18\" /> which can easily be checked by hand.\n</p><p><br />\nThe answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/d/0dd2d06cecfc4988d1f3f1e555fcd71e8c620a53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{111}{121}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME\" title=\"1979 AHSME\">1979 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1979 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1979\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">Problem 26</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" row